# Explainable 3D Deep Learning vs. Classical Machine Learning for Lung Nodule Malignancy Prediction on LIDC-IDRI

An end-to-end volumetric classification and explainable artificial intelligence (XAI) framework on thoracic computed tomography (CT) scans from the **LIDC-IDRI** (Lung Image Database Consortium and Image Database Resource Initiative) cohort.

---

## 1. Project Overview & Problem Statement

Early characterization of pulmonary nodules is essential for effective lung cancer intervention. This project implements a **3D binary classification pipeline** that distinguishes between **Benign (`0`)** and **Malignant (`1`)** nodules using volumetric CT sub-volumes from the LIDC-IDRI dataset.

Rather than relying on an uninterpretable black box, this project benchmarks a **Classical Machine Learning baseline** (Random Forest trained on 15 morphological and first-order intensity statistics) against an end-to-end **Volumetric Deep Learning model** (adapted 3D ResNet-18). Spatial decision plausibility is clinically verified using **3D Gradient-weighted Class Activation Mapping (Grad-CAM)** overlaid directly onto central axial CT planes.

### Exact Input and Output Formats

- **Input:**
  - **For 3D CNN:** A single-channel 3D volumetric tensor of shape $1 \times 32 \times 32 \times 32$ (Depth, Height, Width in voxels, lung-windowed to $[-1000, 400]\text{ HU}$ and min-max scaled to $[0.0, 1.0]$).
  - **For Classical ML Baseline:** A 1D feature vector of 15 radiologist-annotated morphological attributes and 3D intensity summary statistics extracted from the $32^3$ region of interest (ROI).
  - **For Custom Inference:** Supports `.npy` 3D volumes, `.nii` / `.nii.gz` CT scans, and 2D `.png` / `.jpg` slices.
- **Output:**
  - Diagnostic class prediction: **Benign (`0`)** or **Malignant (`1`)**.
  - Malignancy probability $p \in [0.0, 1.0]$ and model confidence score.
  - A $32 \times 32 \times 32$ 3D Grad-CAM activation heatmap overlaid on the central axial CT slice.

---

## 2. End-to-End Pipeline Architecture

```
[Raw LIDC-IDRI Cohort (1,176 NIfTI 3D Patches)]
                         │
                         ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ STAGE 1: DATASET CURATION & LEAKAGE-FREE SPLIT              │
│ - Parse 1,176 NIfTI sub-volumes & metadata dictionaries     │
│ - Consolidate radiologist malignancy scores (1 to 5 scale)  │
│ - Exclude indeterminate cases (mean score == 3.0)           │
│ - Axial reorientation: (128, 128, 64) -> (64, 128, 128)     │
│ - Center crop to 32×32×32 voxel regions of interest (ROIs)  │
│ - Lung windowing: [-1000, 400] HU -> Min-Max scaled [0, 1]  │
│ - SeriesInstanceUID Grouped Split (70% Train, 15% Val, 15% Test)│
└──────────────┬──────────────────────────────┬───────────────┘
               │                              │
               ▼                              ▼
┌──────────────────────────────┐ ┌──────────────────────────────┐
│ STAGE 2A: CLASSICAL BASELINE │ │ STAGE 2B: 3D DEEP LEARNING   │
│ - 15 Tabular Morphological & │ │ - 1×32×32×32 Volumetric Tensor│
│   Intensity HU Descriptors   │ │ - 3D ResNet-18 (r3d_18)      │
│ - Balanced Random Forest     │ │ - BCEWithLogitsLoss + Adam   │
│   Classifier (150 trees)     │ │ - Data Augmentation (Flips,  │
│                              │ │   In-plane 90° Rotations)    │
└──────────────┬───────────────┘ └──────────────┬───────────────┘
               │                                │
               └───────────────┬────────────────┘
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ STAGE 3: EXPLAINABLE AI (XAI) & EVALUATION                  │
│ - Comparative Test Metrics: Accuracy, ROC-AUC, Sensitivity, │
│   Specificity, Precision, and F1-Score                      │
│ - Hook into 3D ResNet-18 layer4 residual blocks             │
│ - Generate 3D Grad-CAM volumetric activation maps           │
│ - Alpha-blended visual overlay on central axial CT slices   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

